Terminal 1

Type cd kafka - to navigate into kafka Directory.

Start the Kafka environment

step 1 - To Generate a Cluster UUID
KAFKA_CLUSTER_ID="$(bin/kafka-storage.sh random-uuid)"

step 2 - To Format Log Directories
bin/kafka-storage.sh format --standalone -t $KAFKA_CLUSTER_ID -c config/server.properties

step 3 - Start the Kafka Server
bin/kafka-server-start.sh config/server.properties



Terminal 2

Type cd kafka - to navigate into kafka Directory.

Create a topic to store your events

step 4 - bin/kafka-topics.sh --create --topic quickstart-events --bootstrap-server localhost:9092

step 5 - bin/kafka-topics.sh --describe --topic quickstart-events --bootstrap-server localhost:9092


Write some events into the topic

step 6 - Producer
bin/kafka-console-producer.sh --topic quickstart-events --bootstrap-server localhost:9092
